# Produce vector-preserving PDF

## Scope and existing evidence

Historical evidence is domain structure, not an operating raster or PDF
renderer; the finite design acceptance is explicitly bounded.

Embed bounded texture and image resources, preserve physical page boxes and
color, retain searchable semantics when compatible, and emit a render manifest.

Current executable evidence now freezes the transport-neutral render-manifest
input structure required by the accepted reproducibility contract. It retains
accepted revision/document/profile/paper identities, asset identities, engine
version, model choices, variation seed, material authority, renderer version,
quality profile, and output-affecting render options. A 2,880-state exhaustive
oracle crosses all 120 orders of five assets with all 24 orders of four model
choices while requiring every scalar reproducibility input to remain exact.

Render identity computation, serialization, PDF bytes, resource embedding,
searchable-text policy, and file commit remain open.

A transport-neutral PDF composition plan now also preserves final page order,
caller-owned physical page boxes, vector authority, color intent, explicit
searchable-semantic-text disposition, explicit embedded-versus-safe-reference
asset disposition, and render-manifest linkage. An 18,432-state exhaustive
oracle crosses all 24 orders of four pages, all 16 searchable-text masks, all
six orders of three assets, and all eight asset-disposition masks while
requiring exact caller authority to survive unchanged.

PDF object encoding, fonts, compression, concrete safe-reference policy,
compatibility decisions, resource bytes, serialization, and file commit remain
open.

## Finite one-page vector-preserving PDF Export contract

**Inputs:** a fully admitted one-page A4 vector plan, actual source assets,
selected profile/handwriting evidence, physical paper geometry, accepted
revision, deterministic quality/material identity and explicit Export intent.
**Outputs:** a proposed complete PDF byte artifact with a reproducibility
manifest and exact authorized destination receipt, or an all-or-nothing
refusal. Rendering a preview never authorizes a filesystem write.

**One-page content:** page `p1`, `210 x 297 mm`, contains title text `t1`
(`Biología`), body text `t2`, an equation `e1` (`x² + 1 = 2`), a 2 x 2 table
`tab1` and black vector leaf line art `f1`. Preserve centerline/contour,
rule, mathematical and table path geometry as vector PDF drawing operations
in physical page units. Declare the page MediaBox/CropBox from accepted
paper bounds with an exact mm-to-PDF-point transform; no browser screenshot
or arbitrary raster whole-page fallback is allowed.

**Resources and exceptions (proposed bounds):** embed referenced image assets
only after byte integrity/media validation, at most 16 MiB per image and
64 MiB total resources per page. Paper texture may be a bounded separate
raster layer, never a replacement for text/diagram vectors.

Font glyphs
requiring a non-embeddable or unavailable font refuse searchable text until a
selected admissible mapping exists. If handwriting is outlines only,
retain searchable semantics only where exact Unicode-to-path ownership can
be proved; otherwise explicitly report `SearchabilityUnavailable`, not a
fabricated invisible text overlay. Declare resolved color intent, not a
printer color guarantee.

**Reproducibility manifest:** bind exact document/revision, source IDs,
profile ID and revision, paper/asset IDs, renderer/engine version, variation
seed, material preset, quality profile, resource digests and output-affecting
options. Produce the manifest as inspectable Export metadata; a changed
asset, seed, page or output option changes render identity and invalidates
cached PDF bytes. A successful byte plan is not yet an authorized destination
commit. Never write a partially constructed PDF after validation failure.

**Worked example:** the A4 five-object content yields a PDF plan with vector
strokes for `t1`, `e1`, `tab1` and `f1`, plus a bounded paper-texture resource
when explicitly selected. The render manifest points to accepted revision
`r18` and a selected deterministic seed; `t2` remains searchable only if the
exact Unicode mapping is supported. The page keeps `210 x 297 mm` regardless
of Preview/Final resolution. This specifies the artifact but does not emit
PDF bytes in the present implementation.

**Refusal example:** an image digest mismatch, incomplete glyph coverage,
out-of-page table, unknown media decoder, missing exact text mapping when
searchability is mandatory, or resource budget exceeded blocks Export.
No partial PDF, silent rasterization of every page, path overwrite, or
misleading Searchable=true result is permitted.

**Assumptions and limits:** typed render manifest and PDF composition plan
preserve page order, source assets, vector/color intent and explicit
searchability disposition. Real PDF object encoding, font embedding, image
bytes, render identity, accepted Export file commit and print fidelity remain
unimplemented. This acceptance is theoretical for PDF output itself.

## Acceptance decision

- **Basis:** practical for reproducibility/PDF plan data structures;
  theoretical for complete PDF bytes and authorized Export, 2026-11-02.
- **Delivered:** one text/equation/table/line-art A4 page, resource bounds,
  explicit searchability/raster exceptions, manifest and refusal gates.
- **Not implemented by this acceptance:** actual vector PDF emitter,
  font/resource embedding, file Export or print certification.
